Three dashboards lacked the time-based greeting feature present in web Buyer/Seller dashboards, creating inconsistent UX.

## Changes

- **Admin Dashboard** (`admin/src/components/AdminDashboard.tsx`): Added greeting state with useEffect hook, displays "Good Morning/Afternoon/Evening, {fullName}"
- **Mobile Buyer Dashboard** (`frontend/src/mobile/src/screens/buyer/BuyerDashboardScreen.tsx`): Added `getGreeting()` function, replaced "Welcome back" with time-based greeting
- **Mobile Seller Dashboard** (`frontend/src/mobile/src/screens/seller/SellerDashboardScreen.tsx`): Added `getGreeting()` function, replaced "Seller Dashboard" with time-based greeting

## Implementation

Web dashboards use useState pattern:
```typescript
const [greeting, setGreeting] = useState('');

useEffect(() => {
  const hour = new Date().getHours();
  if (hour < 12) setGreeting('Good Morning');
  else if (hour < 18) setGreeting('Good Afternoon');
  else setGreeting('Good Evening');
}, []);
```

Mobile dashboards use function pattern:
```typescript
const getGreeting = () => {
  const hour = new Date().getHours();
  if (hour < 12) return 'Good Morning';
  else if (hour < 18) return 'Good Afternoon';
  else return 'Good Evening';
};
```

Greeting logic: Morning (< 12), Afternoon (12-18), Evening (> 18).

