The `Game Time` column sorted lexicographically, causing `12:15PM` to appear after `1:00PM ET` since string comparison treats `'1' < '12'`.

## Changes

- **`docs/index.html` — `renderTable()` sort block**: Special-cases `key === 'Game Time'` to sort by parsed UTC timestamps via the existing `parseGameTimeET()` helper instead of `localeCompare`. Unparseable/missing times are pushed to the bottom in both sort directions.

```js
if (key === 'Game Time') {
  const da = parseGameTimeET(a['Game Time']);
  const db = parseGameTimeET(b['Game Time']);

  if (!da && !db) return 0;
  if (!da) return 1;   // unparseable → bottom, regardless of direction
  if (!db) return -1;

  const diff = da.getTime() - db.getTime();
  return sortConfig.direction === 'asc' ? diff : -diff;
}
```

All other columns retain their existing sort behavior.

