Bochs BIOS reads the ATA Error register immediately after SRST to confirm a drive exists. Per the ATA spec, the master must hold `0x01` (Diagnostic Passed) post-reset; our code left it at `0x00` (None), causing Bochs to reject the drive as "unknown device" and INT 13h to fail every subsequent read.

## Changes

- **`HardDrive.Reset()`** — set `Error = DeviceError.DiagnosticPassed` after `SetIdleState()` so the register holds `0x01` before Bochs reads it
- **`ATA.HandleDeviceControlWrite()`** — set `DiagnosticPassed` on each drive when SRST is deasserted, keeping the live register consistent with the spec
- **`CdRomDrive.Reset()`** — same fix; the ATA spec applies equally to ATAPI masters
- **`Machine.cs`** — remove the dead `var hdd = new HardDrive(path)` that opened the disk image a second time and leaked the `FileStream` without ever using it

```csharp
public override void Reset()
{
    SetIdleState();
    // ATA spec: master must present 0x01 (Diagnostic Passed) after SRST.
    // Bochs BIOS rejects the drive as "unknown device" if this is 0x00.
    Error = DeviceError.DiagnosticPassed;
    ...
}
```

